<blockquote>
Then the wolf embraced the child, for wolves can be loving too. In her embrace, the boy felt himself returned to the womb. When he awoke, his legs felt no different.<br>
"You have kept me alive one more night great wolf, what good will that do?"<br>
"You must help yourself. I will teach you."<br>
"Oh yes. I would love to be taught!" said the boy.<br>
The wolf wrestled with the boy every day until he was much stronger. They went hunting for food together, the boy upon Imhorta's back. Then the boy found wood, and fixed it to his legs so that he could cross the snow.
